[Music]  hey it's your girl miko i'm a food  vlogger over at mikko in the dish and  today tasty has challenged me to use  every item in my fridge to make a  charcuterie board so i'm about to empty  out this fridge behind me and we are  about to make the ultimate charcuterie  board follow along and watch me as i  make this floor  all right so i have my waffle iron  already preheated i sprayed it a little  bit with some cooking oil and all i have  to do is take my biscuit and put it  right on the grate i'm going to close it  and let it cook for three to four  minutes they look beautiful they're  golden brown add my butter here  i also have some fresh fruit that i  found in the fridge so i'm gonna add  some strawberries  some blueberries and got some really  juicy blackberries we're gonna make a  very delicious light and airy fruit dip  so i already have cream cheese in a bowl  i'm going to basically mix this into  it's really light and fluffy now it  looks perfect i'm going to start adding  my remaining ingredients  powdered sugar  i'm going to add just a little bit of  vanilla  now that all the ingredients are in i'm  going to start to whip this until  everything is nice and smooth so i'm  going to add this to a bowl that'll be  good for the sharp creatory board  i'm going to put that right here for now  and so that we can make diy parfaits i  grabbed a little bit of granola that i  had in the pantry so i also had in my  fridge some greek yogurt that's perfect  to go with our breakfast charcuterie  board and it also fits really well with  the sweet side of our board and the way  i'm thinking about setting this up is i  really want to make sure  that the colors or the light colors are  separated so that your eye moves  throughout the board it's looking good  so far we're going to continue to build  up the sweet side and then we'll  eventually get to the savory side i was  able to brown up some mashed potatoes  from last night's dinner and tasty  happens to have a really delicious  looking donut recipe made from mashed  potatoes let's jump right into the  recipe i'm going to add to my flour some  baking powder baking soda  salt  and nutmeg  add in all of my ingredients  coming through nice and evenly now let's  jump into our wet ingredients i have  some room temperature butter here and  i'm going to actually cream until it's  nice and smooth we're going to continue  the creaming by adding in some  granulated sugar brown sugar  and those leftover mashed potatoes i was  telling you about  let's get to freezing  all right that looks good so i have some  eggs i'm going to add the mix  and some vanilla  all right so this batter is coming  together really nicely next i'm going to  do is those dry ingredients that we  first sifted i'm going to add half of  that into the batter so there we go  i'm going to mix this in all together  now i'm going to add my buttermilk  [Music]  that looks good and now i'm going to add  in the rest of my drink  and now i'm going to use a spatula  actually to fold in the remaining dry  ingredients all right our dough is  looking good  get a little bit of flour  now flour is really important because  it's going to keep the dough from  sticking to your surface it's going to  keep the dough from sticking to your  hand you're going to probably add  anywhere from two tablespoons to a  quarter cup of flour as you're kneading  all right our dough looks good it's come  together really nicely now i'm going to  take a rolling pin and we're basically  going to roll this out to about a half  an inch  now we're going to cut our dough i have  a three inch cutter that i'm going to  use so we're going to just press that  straight down and lift up i'm going to  do that all around the entire dough  now i can just lift up my scraps from  around my donut now i'm going to take a  smaller 1 inch cutter and then i'm going  to basically do the same thing in the  very center of each of these donut  circles all right so our oil is ready we  have to wait for it to get to 375  degrees fahrenheit we basically want  these to  be in there  for two minutes on each side  and you can see there are beautiful  beautiful golden brown all right the  donuts look really good i'm going to go  ahead and take these out and i'm going  to add them to a wire rack  and we're going to make a quick cinnamon  sugar just by adding a little cinnamon  to some sugar  i'll stir that up to make sure  everything's equally incorporated it  takes my donut and basically dump it  right inside give it a little bit of  shake and now we have a delicious  cinnamon sugar topping for our donut so  we just wrapped up making these  delicious mashed potato donuts using our  leftover mashed potatoes to complete our  sweet side of the board i have some  peanut butter that i pulled out of the  fridge and i'm going to place this right  here  and i have some leftover peach chutney i  actually made a peach cobbler had a  bunch of peaches left  the sweet pot is looking nice and decked  out but i still have a ton of items that  i need to figure out don't have to make  a vegan maple sausage that is actually  what we're going to use  so i have a little maple syrup  got our black pepper  sage  thyme  garlic powder  and our sauce  i'm going to throw on some gloves to  help me mix this all together  get right in there and basically what i  want to do now is i want to divide this  into eight equal parts in order to make  some pan patties so i'm going to  basically just do a nice soft press into  a little bitty sausage patty just like  that and then add my sausage patty right  inside i'm gonna go ahead and flip these  over we'll give these another two to  three minutes and then they're ready to  go onto our board in order to help with  not staining the board is add a little  bit of paper down first that also is  going to provide some color and some fun  texture that is very interesting to the  eye i love to have a range of cheese  inside of my fridge so we'll add some of  those pieces here as well so let's go  ahead and get right into the candied  beef bacon recipe i went ahead and  created a single layer of all of the  bacon i'm gonna pop that into the oven  my complete house smells like bacon i  can tell that it's ready to pull out  we're gonna  get this pepper jelly that i found in  the fridge it's gonna be really good in  order to add not only some sweetness but  also some spiciness it's nice and  lacquered up with this jelly and so what  i'm going to do is throw this back into  the oven for another three to five  minutes so our candied bacon turned out  phenomenal you can see it's glistening  and all lacquered up with that pepper  jelly i am super impressed already at  what we've been able to do  so i had some deli meat this  traditionally goes into a charcoalery  board and i'll add those throughout the  board as well i am truly working through  all the items in my fridge the last  leftover i have is a steak from last  night's dinner with hubby all i'm gonna  do is add my steak to a  wire  wrap on top of a baking sheet i have my  oven preheated to 250 degrees fahrenheit  i actually had some leftover coffee  butter i know that sounds odd coffee and  steak goes great together i'm gonna add  about two tablespoons of that to my  skillet i'm gonna let that heat up and  then i'm also going to continue to add  my steak into the skillet and then we're  going to let that cook into the coffee  butter give it a little jiggle just to  make sure we're getting all that coffee  butter from the bottom  add it to our wire rack and we don't  want this coffee butter to go away so  we're just going to add what little bit  is left over the top  i'm so excited to add this to my  charcuterie board  boom  and we have coffee butter steak we've  got some spaces to fill in i actually  happen to have some leftover boiled eggs  we have some deli meats that we already  added from the fridge so in the pantry i  went ahead and grabbed a couple crackers  this is truly the ultimate board look at  this i'm actually quite impressed at how  well we did all right if i'm being  completely honest this is what i've been  waiting for  that is incredibly moist on the inside  don't even imagine that you're tasting  mashed potatoes this tastes like a  traditional cake doughnut where do i go  next how about bacon  let me tell you something this bacon  is nice it's crispy and that pepper  jelly is so good it provides that heat  and that sweet is exactly what i need i  am in heaven this is so good first of  all i want to thank you guys for  sticking with me for this full  gargantuan board if you want to see me  make more charcuterie boards here on  tasty leave a comment below let me know  i'm miko and until next time  oh yes  [Music]  you

